# SAMPLE ONLY - not a real key.
#
# Private key of the feed server TLS certificate, used when
# FEED_DISTRIBUTOR_HTTPS_ENABLED=true.
#
# What to do:
#   1. Put the private key in this folder as "server.key" (no ".sample").
#      The folder is mounted read-only at /certs, so the default setting
#      FEED_DISTRIBUTOR_TLS_KEY_FILE=/certs/server.key finds it.
#   2. Make it readable by UID 10001 (the container user) only, e.g.:
#        sudo chown 10001 server.key && chmod 600 server.key
#   3. Delete this sample file if you like; it is never read.
#
# Format: PEM text (Base64 between BEGIN and END PRIVATE KEY lines), RSA or EC.
# It must NOT be password-protected: the server cannot prompt for a passphrase.
# To remove one:  openssl pkey -in encrypted.key -out server.key
#
# It must match server.crt. These two commands must print the same value:
#   openssl x509 -in server.crt -noout -pubkey | openssl sha256
#   openssl pkey -in server.key -pubout       | openssl sha256
#
# Never commit this file or include it in a backup or archive.
